s not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that specifies an id reference."}]}],"name":"id"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Indicates the type of pedal mark, such as start, stop, sostenuto, or change."}]}],"name":"kind"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Distinguishes multiple pedals occurring simultaneously."}]}],"name":"number"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether pedal lines are used."}]}],"name":"usesLines"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether Ped, Sost, and * signs are used."}]}],"name":"usesSigns"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether the short P and S signs are used instead of the full Ped and Sost signs, when the sign attribute is set and the type is start or sostenuto."}]}],"name":"isAbbreviated"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways."}]}],"name":"position"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font."}]}],"name":"font"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}]}],"name":"color"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different. The most typical case is for credits, such as:"}]}],"name":"halign"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The valign attribute is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the text. Defaults are implementation-dependent."}]}],"name":"valign"}],"kind":"parameters"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/init(id:kind:number:usesLines:usesSigns:isAbbreviated:position:font:color:halign:valign:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLValign":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLValign"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValign","title":"MXLValign","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLValign"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The valign type is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the text. If"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the text is on multiple lines, baseline alignment refers to the baseline of the lowest line of text. Defaults"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are implementation-dependent."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlvalign"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The pedal type represents piano pedal marks, including damper and sostenuto pedal marks. The line attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yes if pedal lines are used. The sign attribute is yes if Ped, Sost, and * signs are used. For compatibility"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with older versions, the sign attribute is yes by default if the line attribute is no, and is no by default if"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the line attribute is yes. If the sign attribute is set to yes and the type is start or sostenuto, the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"abbreviated attribute is yes if the short P and S signs are used, and no if the full Ped and Sost signs are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"used. It is no by default. Otherwise the abbreviated attribute is ignored. The alignment attributes are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ignored if the sign attribute is no.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPedal","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPedal","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal","title":"MXLPedal"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vs. a music font.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLFont","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal/init(id:kind:number:usesLines:usesSigns:isAbbreviated:position:font:color:halign:valign:)":{"title":"init(id:kind:number:usesLines:usesSigns:isAbbreviated:position:font:color:halign:valign:)","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal\/init(id:kind:number:useslines:usessigns:isabbreviated:position:font:color:halign:valign:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLPedal"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Kind","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLPedalV4KindO"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"usesLines"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"usesSigns"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"isAbbreviated"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"position"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLPosition","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"font"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLFont","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"halign"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"valign"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLValign","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLValignO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?)"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/init(id:kind:number:usesLines:usesSigns:isAbbreviated:position:font:color:halign:valign:)"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLNumberLevel","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLeftCenterRight":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The left-center-right type is used to define horizontal alignment and text justification.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLeftCenterRight","title":"MXLLeftCenterRight","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlleftcenterright"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"abstract":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLPosition","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal/Kind-swift.enum":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal\/kind-swift.enum","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The pedal-type simple type is used to distinguish types of pedal directions. The start value indicates the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"start of a damper pedal, while the sostenuto value indicates the start of a sostenuto pedal. The other values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be used with either the damper or sostenuto pedal. The soft pedal is not included here because there is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no special symbol or graphic used for it beyond what can be specified with words and bracket elements."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum","title":"MXLPedal.Kind"}}}